amol","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5555-7a26-ba01-676067c2c7ea","description":"Morphine","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-5555-7491-819a-3a10df385f59","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What is Hepatology the study of?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"Hepatology focuses on the liver, which also helps filter waste products from the blood.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-5555-755d-afd9-3cea465a4023","description":"The liver","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-5555-7189-a64e-ea539fc7c182","description":"Religion","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5555-78ec-9be7-fa58f287a036","description":"The moon","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5555-7d20-95a5-def255a36a37","description":"The number 7","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-5555-7063-a4cd-4d33f0346d7a","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What is Oology the study of?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"Oology is a branch of ornithology focused on bird eggs, including their shells, shape, and markings.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-5555-7002-a7d1-3c510328440a","description":"eggs","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-5555-7d83-b754-dad8e19c9a5b","description":"organic particles, such as bacteria, fungal spores, very small insects and pollen","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5555-7cda-83ff-03bfdd5bb805","description":"genetic differences in relation to the environment","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5555-76f8-97c6-993f673d609e","description":"the structure of cells","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-5555-7565-a865-de3c98a55f40","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"Which ancient Greek scholar calculated the circumference of the Earth around 240 BC?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"Eratosthenes compared the Sun\'s angle at Alexandria with its nearly overhead position at Syene, then used the distance between the cities to estimate Earth\'s circumference.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-5555-705c-ac6f-ec21287f2ad5","description":"Eratosthenes","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-5555-7c78-8d40-c2cc5bb61915","description":"Euclid","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5555-775d-b404-d95a8674a39d","description":"Ptolemy","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5555-70e2-8d3b-4dc126f442f0","description":"Hipparchus","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-5555-7d9a-b1e5-a33ba8ddb76a","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"Which American physicist built the first working laser in 1960, using a ruby crystal?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"Theodore Maiman\'s ruby laser used a flash lamp to excite the crystal, producing brief pulses of red light.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-5555-7e50-b158-de26f7cf6544","description":"Theodore Maiman","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-5555-71bc-af0a-4f1490a78b5c","description":"Charles Townes","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5555-7741-8a89-9b941db4c409","description":"Gordon Gould","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5555-7260-bef4-6a3938af1301","description":"Arthur Schawlow","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-5555-7432-988a-dd6269cd1639","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"Where can we find the tympanic membrane?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"The tympanic membrane vibrates in response to sound and passes those vibrations to the three small bones in the middle ear.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-5555-7c28-bd95-dc1b5e82014a","description":"Ear","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-5555-7bc1-86fa-4ee40bed0fc6","description":"Nose","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5555-718d-923d-f9ce797ee4a2","description":"Mouth","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5555-7461-9900-84cb229328ec","description":"Eye","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-5555-798a-94c6-f5fddd3769ce","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","questi